<v Eric Kaufman>That basically yanked on enough stuff that it caused breaks in the hull in a couple different places, which-- I knew where a couple of them were. And then some of them actually just proceeded to get worse and worse. And then at that point we started having a lot of leaking at the hull deck joint on the starboard quarter. Sorry for turning into boat nerd on you, but that's-- I think we ended up maybe about taking on 60 or 70 gallons a day, which isn't really that bad if you think about how quick you can move the bucket if somebody put a gun to your head and said, move that water.
<v Eric Kaufman>那基本上拉扯了足够多的东西，导致船体在几个不同的地方出现了裂缝，其中一些地方我知道在哪儿。然后有些实际上就开始变得越来越严重。然后在那一刻，我们开始在右舷四分之一处的船体甲板接缝处大量进水。抱歉对你变得这么“船极客”，但我认为我们最终可能每天进水60到70加仑，如果你想一下，如果有人拿枪指着你的头让你把水舀出去，你移动桶的速度有多快，这其实并不算太糟。

00:11:12.640 --> 00:11:20.870
<v Ira Glass>He had a big, heavy manual pump on board that pumped a gallon with each stroke. So 60 to 70 gallons took a few minutes. No biggie.
<v Ira Glass>他船上有一个又大又沉的手动泵，每按一次能泵出一加仑。所以60到70加仑只需要几分钟。没什么大不了的。

00:11:20.870 --> 00:11:31.890
<v Ira Glass>Yeah. The boat's not going to sink at that point. We're not all going to die because we've got a bunch of water coming in. It's a pain in the ass, but it's not the end of the world. There you are. It was under control.
