00:12:00.140 --> 00:12:26.940
<v Charlotte Kaufman>Kids get rashes, so we didn't freak out. But then her ears started to smell like cheese. At first we thought it was because we weren't bathing enough. We were all pretty dirty. So we cleaned her ears up, and they still smelled like cheese. So now we've got two things going on. And then she started getting diarrhea. And then she started acting lethargic. And when your kid starts to act differently, that's when you need to really pay attention.
<v Charlotte Kaufman>孩子起皮疹很正常，所以我们没惊慌。但后来她的耳朵开始闻起来像奶酪。起初我们以为是因为我们洗澡不够。我们大家都挺脏的。所以我们清理了她的耳朵，但它们仍然闻起来像奶酪。现在我们遇到了两件事。然后她开始腹泻。接着她开始变得萎靡不振。当你的孩子开始表现不同时，那就是你需要真正注意的时候。

00:12:26.940 --> 00:12:39.930
<v Ira Glass>So they got on the satellite phone and they called Lyra's doctor. And he said to give her amoxicillin, an antibiotic. Which they do for a couple days, and it doesn't work. The kid's still sick. And now they don't know how worried they should be.
<v Ira Glass>所以他们拨通了卫星电话，呼叫了莱拉的医生。他说给她服用阿莫西林，一种抗生素。他们给喂了两天，但这没用。孩子还是病着。现在他们不知道应该有多担心。

00:12:39.930 --> 00:12:46.910
<v Charlotte Kaufman>With kids, within 24 hours you should see results with antibiotics. And there was no improvement.
