00:12:46.910 --> 00:13:04.770
<v Ira Glass>Now the two days that Lyra is taking antibiotics are the same two days that the boat enters those rough seas where they're getting broached and water starts to leak in. And so, on the morning of their 16th day at sea, Eric decides, as safety precaution, to advise the Coast Guard of what is happening, just in case things go south.
<v Ira Glass>现在莱拉服用抗生素的那两天，也是船只进入波涛汹涌的海域，遭受横推并开始漏水的那两天。因此，在海上第16天的早晨，埃里克决定作为安全预防措施，通知海岸警卫队发生了什么，以防万一情况变糟。

00:13:04.770 --> 00:13:17.830
<v Eric Kaufman>We're just going to let them know, hey, this is the situation, this is our medical situation, this is who's on board, this is the sea state we're at right now, so that if this gets any worse, they have some context of what's actually happening.
<v Eric Kaufman>我们只是要让他们知道，嘿，这就是情况，这就是我们的医疗状况，这是船上的人，这是我们现在的海况，以便如果情况变得更糟，他们对实际上发生了什么有具体的背景了解。

00:13:17.830 --> 00:13:22.660
<v Charlotte Kaufman>And he called them with our satellite phone and gave them that update.
<v Charlotte Kaufman>他用卫星电话打给他们，并提供了那个更新。

00:13:22.660 --> 00:13:30.990
<v Eric Kaufman>--which, in the Maritime world, it's not the most common thing to do, but it's certainly smiled upon to do that.
