<v Charlotte Kaufman>And then you wait. There's nothing, no magical sparkles that come out. There's nothing that says, we got it. We got your message. You just have to trust that somebody, somewhere, in front of a computer is getting this message and it's going to help coordinate getting you help.
<v Charlotte Kaufman>然后你等待。没有什么神奇的火花冒出来。没有任何东西说，我们收到了。我们收到你的信息了。你只能相信某个地方、某台电脑前的人正在收到这条信息，并将协调为你提供帮助。

