<v Ira Glass>So that was in the morning of their 16th day at sea that they pushed the button on the EPIRB. It took until near sunset for anything to happen. First there was a burst of static on the radio, which they thought was dead, the radio. They hadn't heard anything from anybody on it in a week. It was a plane with rescuers saying they were on their way.
<v Ira Glass>所以那是在他们海上第16天的早晨，他们按下了EPIRB上的按钮。直到日落时分才发生了一些事情。首先无线电中传来一阵静电噪声，他们以为那东西坏了，无线电。他们已经一周没在上面听到任何人的声音了。那是一架救援飞机的声音，说他们正在赶来。

