<v Maya>所以你把她带来了。加兰特·福克斯（Gallant Fox）、奥马哈（Omaha）、战将（War Admiral）。

00:44:56.510 --> 00:45:12.880
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Around eight years old, the dinosaur obsession switched to horses, and it's been horses ever since then. A lot of girls love horses-- Maya loves race horses. Maya is now 13, and she will walk right up to you with her pad of paper and just begin talking.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>大约八岁时，对恐龙的痴迷转向了马，从那时起就一直离不开马。很多女孩喜欢马——玛雅喜欢赛马。玛雅现在13岁了，她会带着她的记事本直接走向你，然后就开始说话。

00:45:12.880 --> 00:45:18.070
<v Maya>516, [INAUDIBLE] Painter, Optimizer.
<v Maya>516，[听不清] 画家，优化者。

00:45:18.070 --> 00:45:53.260
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>It's hard to tell if the obsession with horses is more intense or if it's the same as it was with dinosaurs. Only now it strikes people as a weird instead of cute. It strikes people, as it may have struck you, that Maya has autism. For technical reasons, Maya's never been diagnosed as on the autism spectrum, but she does exhibit almost all the characteristics, including sensitivity to touch, lack of eye contact, obsessive and intense interest in one topic, and difficulty with social emotional reciprocity, what many of us call conversation.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>很难说对马的痴迷是否更强烈，还是和恐龙时期一样。只是现在人们觉得它怪怪的，而不是可爱。人们觉得——就像你们可能觉得的那样——玛雅有自闭症。由于技术原因，玛雅从未被诊断为自闭症谱系，但她确实表现出几乎所有的特征，包括对触觉敏感、缺乏目光接触、对一个话题有强迫性和强烈的兴趣，以及在社会情感互惠方面有困难，即我们许多人所说的对话。

00:45:53.260 --> 00:45:54.770
<v Maya>Man o' War, [INAUDIBLE].
<v Maya>战马（Man o' War），[听不清]。

00:45:54.770 --> 00:45:56.360
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>What is this that you're reading to me?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>你读给我听的这是什么？

00:45:56.360 --> 00:45:57.680
<v Maya>Race horse names.
<v Maya>赛马的名字。

00:45:57.680 --> 00:46:01.420
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>But just every race horse that you've ever heard of?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>但这只是你听说过的每一匹赛马吗？

00:46:01.420 --> 00:46:17.580
<v Maya>Well, the first page, Sir Barton to Affirmed, those 11 are the Triple Crown winners in the United States. Street Life to My Adonis, those are the horses--
<v Maya>嗯，第一页，从“巴顿爵士”（Sir Barton）到“肯定”（Affirmed），那11匹是美国的三冠王冠军。从“街头生活”（Street Life）到“我的阿多尼斯”（My Adonis），那些是马——

00:46:17.580 --> 00:46:33.460
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Maya can tell you every horse that's won the Triple Crown since 1919, their results, their injuries. She tracks the major awards, such as the Eclipse Award which is comprised of more than a dozen categories, which she will recite unprompted over a snack of Doritos.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>玛雅可以告诉你自1919年以来赢得三冠王的每一匹马，它们的比赛结果，它们的伤病情况。她追踪重大奖项，例如Eclipse奖，该奖项由十几个类别组成，她会在吃多力多滋零食时即兴背诵出来。

00:46:33.460 --> 00:46:47.010
<v Maya>Three-year-old male, three-year-old female, older male. And then there's the categories for people, which I don't find as interesting.
<v Maya>三岁雄性，三岁雌性，年长雄性。然后是针对人的类别，我觉得那些没那么有趣。

00:46:47.010 --> 00:46:48.510
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>You don't find the categories for people interesting?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>你觉得针对人的类别不有趣？

00:46:48.510 --> 00:46:49.030
<v Maya>No.
<v Maya>不。

00:46:49.030 --> 00:46:53.420
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Why not?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>为什么不？

00:46:53.420 --> 00:47:01.200
<v Maya>Because the people aren't horses.
<v Maya>因为人不是马。

00:47:01.200 --> 00:47:23.420
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>People have always been hard for Maya. In preschool, kindergarten, she never really made friends. We figured she just wasn't interested. But as she got older, it became clear it was the other children who weren't interested in her. First grade, second grade, third grade, the only time Maya ever got invited to someone's house was when the entire class was invited.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>人们对玛雅来说总是很难相处。在学前班、幼儿园，她从来没真正交到朋友。我们以为她只是不感兴趣。但随着她长大，很明显是其他孩子对她不感兴趣。一年级、二年级、三年级，玛雅唯一一次被邀请去别人家，是因为全班都被邀请了。

00:47:23.420 --> 00:47:52.600
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>In the meantime, Maya amassed a team of therapists who diagnosed her with reactive attachment disorder, RAD. Kids with RAD have often been neglected or abused as babies. They don't emotionally attach to anyone early so they have attachment disorder, which in Maya's case was just one diagnosis to be followed by a series of others that all seemed to take her most obvious character trait and add the word "disorder" to it.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>与此同时，玛雅积攒了一支由治疗师组成的团队，他们诊断她患有反应性依恋障碍（RAD）。患有RAD的孩子通常在婴儿期被忽视或虐待。他们早期没能与任何人建立情感依恋，所以他们有依恋障碍，这在玛雅的案例中只是随后一系列诊断中的一个，所有这些诊断似乎都采用了她最明显的性格特征，并加上了“障碍”这个词。

00:47:52.600 --> 00:48:17.910
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>And true to the label, Maya did not attach to other children, which was so painful to watch. Because it wasn't that she didn't care, she just didn't know how to interact. She didn't know how to have a back and forth. She would ask my mom or Ellen to invite someone over, and that someone would come over, and then they just wouldn't come back or return the invitation. Maya didn't get why her friends were always so busy.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>正如标签所言，玛雅没有与其他孩子建立依恋关系，这看在眼里非常痛苦。因为并不是她不在乎，她只是不知道如何互动。她不知道如何进行来回的互动。她会请求我妈妈或艾伦邀请某人过来，那个人会来，然后他们就是不再来了，也不回送邀请。玛雅不明白为什么她的朋友总是那么忙。

00:48:17.910 --> 00:48:34.330
<v Maya>Well, at school there were kids who would always be playing together as the same group, same people always playing together. And I was never really a part of those groups. I'm more by myself at recess.
<v Maya>嗯，在学校里，有些孩子总是作为同一个群体在一起玩，同样的人总是聚在一起。我从来没真正参与过这些群体。我在休息时间更多是一个人待着。

00:48:34.330 --> 00:48:36.010
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>What do you do at recess?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>休息时间你做什么？

00:48:36.010 --> 00:48:44.250
<v Maya>Draw, play games that don't involve many people.
<v Maya>画画，玩不需要太多人的游戏。

00:48:44.250 --> 00:48:59.830
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>In fourth grade, in a bout of utter boredom, Maya went and knocked on the neighbor's door. She asked if their boys could play. They were busy. And then Maya sat down on their porch and just started wailing, "No one will play with me."
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>四年级时，在极度无聊中，玛雅去敲了邻居的门。她问他们的男孩能不能玩。他们很忙。然后玛雅坐在他们的门廊上开始嚎啕大哭：“没人跟我玩。”

00:48:59.830 --> 00:49:29.040
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>And then things got really dark. She stopped asking for play dates all together. She stopped reading. She stopped smiling, and sleeping. And she was on the edge all the time, especially at school. A kid would take her pencil or brush up against her at the bus stop, and Maya would blow up. She had to be physically restrained. She broke a window. She was diagnosed with oppositional defiant disorder. She got hospitalized for a brief period. Here's my step-mom, Ellen.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>然后事情变得非常糟糕。她完全停止了请求玩耍。她停止了阅读。她停止了微笑和睡觉。她一直处于崩溃边缘，尤其是在学校。一个孩子拿走了她的铅笔或在公共汽车站擦过她，玛雅就会爆发。她必须被物理束缚。她打碎了一扇窗户。她被诊断为对立违抗性障碍。她短暂住院了一段时间。这是我的继母，艾伦。

00:49:29.040 --> 00:49:52.990
<v Ellen>How I felt so helpless. And I had no idea what to do. And none of this [BLEEP] is working. None of it's working. And I'm out of ideas. Like, help. What are we going to do with this kid?
<v Ellen>我感到多么无助。我不知道该怎么办。而且这些 [粗话] 都不起作用。一点用都没有。我没招了。求救。我们要拿这个孩子怎么办？

00:49:52.990 --> 00:50:08.900
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>In our family, we talk about Maya's life in two sections, BC and AC. Everything I've just told you about, that's all BC, before Charlotte. What happened next is AC, after Charlotte. And this is Charlotte.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>在我们家，我们把玛雅的生活分为两个时期，BC和AC。我刚才告诉你的所有这些，那都是BC，Charlotte（夏洛特）之前。接下来发生的是AC，Charlotte之后。这就是Charlotte。

00:50:08.900 --> 00:50:32.910
<v Charlotte>Well, it was the first day of this camp, it was really hot, and we were just waiting for everyone to get there, and we were hanging out. And it was a horse camp, so we were watching these guys throw hay down from a hay loft in the barn. And Maya goes, I did that one time at a place called Hay Down Farm. And we thought that was hilarious for six months.
<v Charlotte>嗯，那是夏令营的第一天，天气真的很热，我们正在等所有人到齐，我们在闲逛。那是马术夏令营，所以我们看着这些人在谷仓的干草棚里扔干草。玛雅说，我在一个叫“干草农场”（Hay Down Farm）的地方做过一次。我们觉得那很有趣，持续了六个月。

00:50:32.910 --> 00:50:50.620
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Hay down. Get it? You do get it? Don't over think it. That is the entire joke. Maya had found her audience. Her audience was Charlotte.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>干草放下（Hay down）。懂了吗？你真的懂了吗？别想太多。这就是整个笑话。玛雅找到了她的听众。她的听众是Charlotte。

00:50:50.620 --> 00:51:21.490
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>As a parent, you try to construct various environments for your kids so that when you have to cast them off on their own, hopefully the right thing will happen. You baby-proof the cabinet so hopefully the baby won't eat poison. You put the kid in a good school and hope she'll learn math. Ellen put Maya in horse camp, but by this point, by the time Maya was 11 years old, a friend was not even on Ellen's list of things to hope for. They'd given up on that. She just wanted to see her kid smile once or twice a week.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>作为父母，你试图为你的孩子构建各种环境，这样当你不得不把他们推向独立时，希望正确的事情会发生。你对柜子做防幼童处理，这样希望婴儿不会吃毒药。你让孩子去好学校，希望她能学会数学。艾伦把玛雅送进了马术夏令营，但到这个时候，到玛雅11岁时，朋友甚至不在艾伦希望的名单上。他们放弃了那点。她只是想每周看到她的孩子笑一两次。

00:51:21.490 --> 00:51:24.270
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>But she dropped Maya off the second day of camp--
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>但第二天她送玛雅去夏令营——

00:51:24.270 --> 00:52:12.590
<v Ellen>And I met Charlotte's mom there. And I said, Maya seems to be kind of connecting with Charlotte. And she said, yeah. Charlotte really is feeling a connection with Maya too. And in fact, she said, Mommy, Maya is perfect. And my jaw practically hit the ground with a thud. I just kept saying it to myself in the car all the way home, Maya is perfect. Mommy, Maya is perfect. I was like, this is not possible. But it is. Her mom said it. It must have really happened.
<v Ellen>我在那里见到了Charlotte的妈妈。我说，玛雅似乎在和Charlotte建立某种联系。她说，是的。Charlotte确实也对玛雅产生了联系。事实上，她说，妈妈，玛雅是完美的。我的下巴几乎重重地掉到了地上。我一直在车里回家的路上对自己重复这句话，玛雅是完美的。妈妈，玛雅是完美的。我心想，这不可能。但这确实发生了。她妈妈说的。它一定真的发生了。

00:52:12.590 --> 00:52:18.550
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>I asked Charlotte recently why Maya was perfect. She told me it was pretty simple, actually.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>我最近问Charlotte为什么玛雅是完美的。她告诉我，这其实很简单。

00:52:18.550 --> 00:52:22.420
<v Charlotte>She was the only girl my age at camp.
<v Charlotte>她是营地里唯一和我同龄的女孩。

00:52:22.420 --> 00:52:23.960
<v Charlotte>Did you like her?
<v Charlotte>你喜欢她吗？

00:52:23.960 --> 00:52:27.830
<v Charlotte>Yeah. It was pretty clear from the beginning that we had a lot of common interests.
<v Charlotte>是的。从一开始就很明显，我们有很多共同兴趣。

00:52:27.830 --> 00:52:29.770
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Like what?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>比如什么？

00:52:29.770 --> 00:52:36.500
<v Charlotte>Horses. Um, yeah.
<v Charlotte>马。嗯，是的。

00:52:36.500 --> 00:53:05.340
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Perfect. Charlotte invited Maya over for a play date that Thursday, just like that. No big deal, just, hey, you want to come over? And she did. Maya went over. And it went fine. There was another play date, and then another, and another. And Charlotte and Maya would sit on the floor together with their model horses. Mostly they did their own thing. They weren't talking or laughing a lot, but we all thought, wow, this is working. Maya has a companion.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>完美。Charlotte邀请玛雅周四去玩耍，就像那样。没什么大不了的，只是，嘿，你想过来玩吗？她去了。玛雅过去了。一切都很顺利。又进行了一次玩耍，然后又一次，又一次。Charlotte和玛雅会坐在地板上一起玩她们的模型马。大多数时候她们各玩各的。她们没有聊很多或笑很多，但我们都心想，哇，这行得通。玛雅有了一个伙伴。

00:53:05.340 --> 00:53:15.900
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>And then a couple months in, they invited Charlotte on an overnight to DC. And afterwards they got a hotel, and Ellen could hear the kids in the other room telling jokes.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>几个月后，她们邀请Charlotte去华盛顿过夜。之后她们开了一间房，艾伦能听到孩子们在隔壁房间讲笑话。

00:53:15.900 --> 00:53:42.550
<v Ellen>And they just cracked up, and Maya lost it, and she just started laughing, and laughing, and laughing. And Charlotte making fart jokes, and Maya just exploding in laughter. And I was lying there in the other room thinking, this is a miracle. I can't believe this is happening. She's giggling and talking and whispering at a sleepover like a regular kid.
<v Ellen>她们只是爆笑，玛雅彻底放开了，她开始笑，笑，笑个不停。Charlotte讲屁笑话，玛雅只是爆发出大笑。我躺在隔壁房间心想，这是一个奇迹。我不敢相信这正在发生。她像个正常的孩子一样在过夜聚会上咯咯笑、说话、耳语。

00:53:42.550 --> 00:53:47.410
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>What would you have imagined Maya would do in that situation?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>你会想象玛雅在这种情况下会做什么？

00:53:47.410 --> 00:54:09.420
<v Ellen>I would have imagined her saying, hey, go to sleep. It's night time. The light is off. I am tired. But that night, Maya discovered what a sleepover could be.
<v Ellen>我会想象她说，嘿，去睡觉。现在是晚上了。灯关了。我累了。但那天晚上，玛雅发现了过夜聚会可以是怎样的。

00:54:09.420 --> 00:54:28.650
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>My mom had a moment like this too, where she realized that AC was a wildly different era than BC. She was watching Maya with Charlotte, and at first she couldn't figure out what was going on with Maya. She looked weird. And then my mom realized, oh, that's happiness.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>我妈妈也有过这样的时刻，她意识到AC是一个与BC截然不同的时代。她在观察玛雅和Charlotte，起初她想不出玛雅怎么了。她看起来怪怪的。然后我妈妈意识到，哦，那是快乐。

00:54:28.650 --> 00:54:51.480
<v Pam>It's just hard to describe how thrilled she was. I felt like Maya would jump out of her skin. AC is just that kind of engagement with somebody else, and engagement in the world. I had hardly seen it in years at all.
<v Pam>很难描述她有多激动。我觉得玛雅会跳出她的皮肤。AC就是那种与他人互动，以及参与到世界中的状态。我几乎已经好几年没见到它了。

00:54:51.480 --> 00:54:54.640
<v Pam>[LAUGHTER]
<v Pam>[笑声]

00:54:54.640 --> 00:55:06.730
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Maya just turned 13 a couple weeks ago. The only thing she wanted for her birthday was a sleepover with Charlotte. So Charlotte came over and the two of them sat on the floor with their model horses for hours.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>玛雅几周前刚满13岁。她生日那天唯一想要的就是和Charlotte过夜。所以Charlotte过来了，她们俩在地板上拿着模型马坐了几个小时。

00:55:06.730 --> 00:55:07.450
<v Charlotte>What's your name?
<v Charlotte>你叫什么名字？

00:55:07.450 --> 00:55:09.390
<v Maya>Sonia.
<v Maya>索尼娅（Sonia）。

00:55:09.390 --> 00:55:10.270
<v Charlotte>What's your name?
<v Charlotte>你叫什么名字？

00:55:10.270 --> 00:55:12.280
<v Maya>I'm Secretariat.
<v Maya>我是“秘书长”（Secretariat）。

00:55:12.280 --> 00:55:24.430
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Charlotte loves to play Hailey, a young rider who's whiny and thinks she knows everything. Maya likes to play, well, Maya, someone who does know everything and can set Hailey in her place.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Charlotte喜欢扮演海莉（Hailey），一个年轻、爱抱怨且认为自己什么都知道的骑手。玛雅喜欢扮演，好吧，玛雅，一个确实什么都知道且能让海莉闭嘴的人。

00:55:24.430 --> 00:55:27.010
<v Charlotte>I've done everything after.
<v Charlotte>我做过之后的一切。

00:55:27.010 --> 00:55:30.540
<v Maya>You haven't Have you raced in the Kentucky Derby?
<v Maya>你没有。你参加过肯塔基德比大赛（Kentucky Derby）吗？

00:55:30.540 --> 00:55:35.950
<v Charlotte>Probably. I don't know. I don't remember. I would've been really little.
<v Charlotte>可能吧。我不知道。我不记得了。我那时候一定非常小。

00:55:35.950 --> 00:55:44.330
<v Maya>I take that as a no. You have not raced in the Kentucky Derby, because really little people do not-- really young people do not race in the Kentucky Derby.
<v Maya>我把它当成否定的回答。你没有参加过肯塔基德比，因为真的小孩子不会——真的年轻人不会参加肯塔基德比。

00:55:44.330 --> 00:55:48.840
<v Charlotte>How do you know I'm not 80-hundred years old and I'm just short because I'm a jockey?
<v Charlotte>你怎么知道我不是8000岁，我只是因为我是骑师才这么矮？

00:55:48.840 --> 00:55:54.620
<v Maya>Oh my gosh. 80-hundred years old. No one's lived to be that old.
<v Maya>哦，天哪。8000岁。没人活到那么大年纪。

00:55:54.620 --> 00:55:57.590
<v Charlotte>How do you know? Have you died yet?
<v Charlotte>你怎么知道？你死了吗？

00:55:57.590 --> 00:55:59.000
<v Maya>No.
<v Maya>没有。

00:55:59.000 --> 00:56:03.830
<v Charlotte>Well then how do you know you're not going to live to 80-hundred years old? Year's old.
<v Charlotte>那你怎么知道你不会活到8000岁？

00:56:03.830 --> 00:56:08.780
<v Maya>Because people just don't live that long.
<v Maya>因为人就是活不了那么久。

00:56:08.780 --> 00:56:23.440
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>That right there, that is a genuine back and forth interaction. Maya is not lecturing, she's not ignoring Charlotte. She's amused. She is feeling amusement. And she's responding directly to what Charlotte is saying.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>就是那一点，那是一个真实的互动交流。玛雅没有在说教，她没有忽视Charlotte。她感到很有趣。她感到了快乐。她正在直接回应Charlotte说的话。

00:56:23.440 --> 00:56:53.360
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Maya and Charlotte have been friends for almost two years now. We'll be two years into AC this summer. And here are the basic facts of AC. Maya no longer regularly gets in trouble at school. She now does her homework and washes her hair without a struggle. She has not had one violent incident AC. She makes eye contact sometimes. She asks, how are you, sometimes. She does chores. That felt impossible BC. All of it seemed impossible BC.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>玛雅和Charlotte做朋友快两年了。今年夏天我们将进入AC的第二年。这是AC的基本事实。玛雅不再在学校定期闯祸。她现在做家庭作业，洗头时也不再挣扎。她在AC期间没有发生过一次暴力事件。她有时会进行目光接触。她有时会问，你好吗。她做家务。在BC时期这感觉是不可能的。BC时这一切看起来都不可能。

00:56:53.360 --> 00:57:28.310
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>The other day I went to pick up Maya from school, and her bus driver got out of the bus to introduce himself to me and tell me, Maya, she's really worked on herself this year. She's doing great. Her horseback riding instructor pulled my mom aside the other day to say, Maya has been making eye contact with me. I've never seen that before. It feels like when people see a really beautiful piece of art and they can't wait to talk to someone about it. Just to say, did you see that? Awesome, right?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>前几天我去学校接玛雅，她的校车司机下车向我自我介绍，告诉我，玛雅，她今年真的很努力改变自己。她做得很好。她的骑马教练前几天把我拉到一边说，玛雅一直在和我进行目光接触。我以前从没见过那样。这感觉就像人们看到一件非常美丽的艺术品，迫不及待地想和某人谈论它。只是想说，你看到了吗？太棒了，对吧？

00:57:28.310 --> 00:57:39.670
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>And Charlotte, I can't imagine a kid better suited to being Maya's friend than Charlotte. Just listen to the way she talks, and try to remember, this kid is 13 years old.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>还有Charlotte，我无法想象一个比Charlotte更适合做玛雅朋友的孩子。只要听听她说话的方式，试着记住，这个孩子才13岁。

00:57:39.670 --> 00:57:42.360
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>How would you describe Maya?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>你会怎么描述玛雅？

00:57:42.360 --> 00:57:46.460
<v Charlotte>She's extremely obsessed with race horses.
<v Charlotte>她极度痴迷于赛马。

00:57:46.460 --> 00:57:48.680
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>What's that been like for you?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>这对你来说意味着什么？

00:57:48.680 --> 00:58:03.580
<v Charlotte>Well, I've learned a lot of new stuff from her actually, because half the time it's all she'll talk about. But it's been really interesting because it's a whole new part of the horse world that I wasn't really familiar with until I met her. You know, all the Triple Crown winners in order.
<v Charlotte>嗯，其实我从她那儿学到了很多新东西，因为有一半时间她只会聊这些。但这真的很有趣，因为这是马术界的一个全新领域，在我遇到她之前我并不太熟悉。你知道，所有的三冠王冠军顺序。

00:58:03.580 --> 00:58:05.930
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>What else do you know about her?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>关于她你还知道什么？

00:58:05.930 --> 00:58:15.590
<v Charlotte>She's really smart. But sometimes she's a bit lacking in social graces. Just a little bit. Sometimes it makes her really funny.
<v Charlotte>她真的很聪明。但有时她有点缺乏社交礼仪。就一点点。有时这让她真的很滑稽。

00:58:15.590 --> 00:58:32.290
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Charlotte's noticed that if she talks about something she's interested in that's not horses, like Star Trek, or Harry Potter, it used to be that Maya just wouldn't respond. She didn't know what to say. But lately, Charlotte says, Maya tries to be interested in whatever she's talking about.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Charlotte注意到，如果她谈论一些她感兴趣的不是马的事情，比如《星际迷航》或《哈利·波特》，过去玛雅只是不会回应。她不知道该说什么。但最近，Charlotte说，玛雅会试着对她谈论的任何事情表现出兴趣。

00:58:32.290 --> 00:58:43.450
<v Charlotte>And sometimes she'll even respond to it by connecting it to horses, which I think is a neat thing to be able to do. I just think it's really cool when people connect everyday things to things that are really their passion.
<v Charlotte>有时她甚至会通过将其与马联系起来来回应，我认为这是一种巧妙的能力。我觉得当人们把日常琐事与真正让他们充满激情的事情联系起来时，真的很酷。

00:58:43.450 --> 00:58:45.350
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Yeah. That's really smart.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>是的。那真的很聪明。

00:58:45.350 --> 00:58:48.260
<v Charlotte>It can be a great way to interact with the world.
<v Charlotte>这可以是与世界互动的一种很好的方式。

00:58:48.260 --> 00:59:02.880
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>When I ask her how she deals with it when Maya has tantrums, Charlotte says, sometimes I wait it out, or sometimes integrating humor can be helpful. See what I mean? That's a special kid. And Maya can see that.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>当我问她当玛雅闹脾气时她是如何处理的，Charlotte说，有时我等它过去，或者有时加入幽默会有帮助。看到我的意思了吗？那是一个特别的孩子。玛雅能看出来。

00:59:02.880 --> 00:59:09.960
<v Maya>This is a really important friendship. And I've been learning how to be a better friend in order to keep the friendship.
<v Maya>这是一个非常重要的友谊。我一直在学习如何成为一个更好的朋友，以维持这段友谊。

00:59:09.960 --> 00:59:12.420
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Like what kinds of things are you learning?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>比如你正在学习什么样的东西？

00:59:12.420 --> 00:59:37.780
<v Maya>Be more flexible. Not just talk about what you want to talk about all the time. Do other stuff that your friend wants. The morning after Maya's birthday sleepover, I found her sitting outside the bedroom door at 6:00 in the morning waiting for Charlotte to wake up. She wasn't allowed to wake her up until 8:00, so Maya was just sitting there.
<v Maya>更灵活。不要总是只谈论你想谈论的事情。做一些你的朋友想做的其他事。玛雅生日过夜后的第二天早晨，我发现她早上6点坐在卧室门外等着Charlotte醒来。她不被允许在8点前吵醒她，所以玛雅只是坐在那里。

00:59:37.780 --> 00:59:59.290
<v Maya>I don't think I'd completely gotten this until I saw Maya waiting-- Maya loves Charlotte. She loves her. She feels the feelings that come when you're a girl and you have a friend who makes you laugh, and thinks about you when you're apart, and gets you. It's not a romantic love, but if you've had this, you know it feels just as important.
<v Maya>直到我看到玛雅在等待时，我才完全明白这一点——玛雅爱Charlotte。她爱她。她感受到了当你是一个女孩，有一个让你发笑的朋友，在你不在时会想到你，并懂你的那种感觉。那不是浪漫的爱，但如果你曾经有过这样的经历，你知道它感觉一样重要。

00:59:59.290 --> 01:00:23.730
<v Maya>Maya is getting to experience the joy of being 13 and having a best friend. And that is why she's willing to work so hard. It's why she's trying to learn how to read facial expressions, and social cues, to control waves of anger and frustration, to sit still when all you want is to wake someone up. You have to really want something to work that hard for it.
<v Maya>玛雅正在体验13岁并拥有一个最好的朋友的快乐。这就是为什么她愿意如此努力。这就是为什么她正在尝试学习如何阅读面部表情、社交线索，控制愤怒和沮丧的浪潮，当你想吵醒某人时坐着不动。你必须真的很想要某样东西才会如此努力。

01:00:23.730 --> 01:00:54.430
<v Maya>Charlotte's going to high school next year and she's just growing up faster than Maya is. She could move on, maybe soon, something we talk about all the time and try not to think about. We know BC, and we know AC, but we don't know what comes after. Maya needed the friendship to learn how to be a friend, but maybe, hopefully, now she knows. And with or without Charlotte, she'll be OK.
<v Maya>Charlotte明年要上高中了，她比玛雅长得快。她可能会搬走，也许很快，这是我们一直谈论但尽量不去想的事情。我们知道BC，我们知道AC，但我们不知道AC之后会是什么。玛雅需要这段友谊来学习如何成为一个朋友，但也许，希望如此，现在她知道了。无论有没有Charlotte，她都会没事的。

01:00:54.430 --> 01:01:19.490
<v Ira Glass>Chana Joffe-Walt is one of the producers of our show.
<v Ira Glass>查娜·乔夫-沃尔特是我们节目的制片人之一。

